{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>Et both his hands.</b> A paradigm for all semikhah ordinances, that they be with both hands." "<b>And he shall confess over it.</b> How does he confess? 'Ana HaShem, I have sinned, I have iniquitated, I have transgressed,' etc., and they answer after him: 'Blessed be the name of His glorious kingdom forever and ever.' I have only their confessions; their acts of coercion, their uncertainties, their inadvertencies — from where? The Talmud says: עונות — for all עונות; פשעיהם — for all פשעים; חטאתם — for all חטאות. The scapegoat designated for Yom HaKippurim atones for intentional defilement of the Sanctuary and its offerings, and for the other transgressions in the Torah, both lenient and stringent: inadvertencies whether known or unknown, positive and negative commandments, karet and court-imposed death penalties — the scapegoat atones. [And he placed them upon the head of the goat verbally.]" "<b>By the hand of a designated man.</b> It is found in the midrash: <b>עתי</b> — whose time has come to die within that year, for the one who carries the goat does not outlive his year. Therefore they would select a man whose time had come to die within that year, and the wisdom of the constellations was easy in their eyes."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:12:54.549622234Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}